	(text "SIROKKO 262.01 MOTOR PWM — DRAFT, NOT INTEGRATED / NOT FOR RELEASE\nSelected topology: high-side P-MOS PWM. Motor M− remains GND_PWR; M+ (large-speed lead only) is switched.\nJ1.3 LOW_PLUS_ISOLATE: terminate and insulate; never connect to +24V or the PWM node.\nThis avoids a low-side topology: no claim that motor common-minus is isolated from chassis is needed."
	(at 40 45 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "54c54b9f-d88e-4b16-a144-40524e98447c")
)
	(text "NORMAL PWM PATH\n+24V_FUSED → RSH1 5mΩ → Q1 IRF5210PbF P-channel → MOTOR_HI_PLUS → motor → GND_PWR.\nQ1: R1 100k G-S = OFF at GPIO Hi-Z/reset/loss of 3V3. Q3 BC817-40 pulls Q1 gate down only from SPEED_CMD GPIO17 via R3=2.2k; D3 BZT52B12 limits |VGS| to 12V.\nPWM rate: 16kHz maximum for this DRAFT. Do NOT use VGS(th) as an ON-rating; Q1 is driven/clamped at about −12V."
	(at 40 160 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "f93e6fe7-0a35-4f02-8b0f-1a359b98d292")
)
	(text "HARDWARE CURRENT CUTOFF — applies to BOTH Q1 PWM and Q4 emergency bypass\nU1 INA300AIDGKR pins: 1 IN+ = RSH_HI; 2 IN− = RSH_LO; 3 LIMIT = R2=2.05k to GND; 4 ENABLE=+3V3; 5 ALERT_N=OCP_TRIP_N; 6 LATCH=+3V3; 7 DELAY floating=10µs; 8 GND; 9 VS=+3V3; 10 HYS=GND=4mV.\nTrip nominal: (20µA×2.05k−0.5mV)/5mΩ = 8.10A; latch must be manually cleared only after root-cause removal.\nOCP_TRIP_N turns Q2 PNP ON: Q1_GATE and FAN_EMERG_GATE return to their P-MOS sources (= OFF)."
	(at 40 190 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "78de77cf-d79b-4f3d-8958-e3419d8d909d")
)
	(text "INDEPENDENT COOLING PATH\nQ4 is a separate IRF5210PbF hard-ON high-side path in parallel with Q1, enabled only by FAN_EMERG_GATE.\nFAN_EMERG_GATE is generated by the independent 24V-powered safety latch/cooldown timer on watchdog/STOP/over-temp fault; it is NOT a GPIO and defaults OFF. It may assert only while OCP_TRIP_N is high. OCP latches Q4 OFF too: emergency fan never bypasses short/locked-rotor protection.\nFAN failure/open circuit is not detected by this circuit; motor locked/short is cut after INA300 detection. A welded Q1/Q4 remains a single-fault not covered by this DRAFT."
	(at 40 225 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "274ac854-7926-4da3-95cf-cc8b946b6c80")
)
	(text "MODE ADMISSION\n1 IDLE / MCU reset / GPIO Hi-Z / logic lost: Q1=OFF, Q4=OFF.  2 PWM RUN: GPIO17 0…16kHz, Q1 only, hardware OCP armed.  3 RECOVERY/STOP/WD/over-temp purge: independent safety timer commands Q4 full ON only if OCP clear.  4 OCP ≥8.10A: latch Q1=Q4=OFF; manual reset after repair.  5 input loss: both OFF; no active purge without energy.\nExcluded: any motor with sustained/pulse current above trip; alternative low-speed lead; automatic restart after OCP; operating after MOSFET short/welded contact."
	(at 230 160 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "58617afa-6404-496e-ba2e-6b2357f314c6")
)
	(text "SUPPRESSION / OPERATIONAL LIMITS\nD1 MBR20100CTG: both Schottky dies in parallel, anode GND_PWR, cathode MOTOR_HI_PLUS; recirculation on Q1/Q4 turn-off. D2 SMCJ43A is across protected 24V bus (VRWM=43V; use its 69.4V maximum clamp at Ipp for margin calculation).\nAdmitted load interface only: 21.6…30V continuous; motor normal current ≤5.21A (125W/24V nameplate); this DRAFT has no established start-current acceptance. INA300 latch ≈8.10A nominal / 10µs qualifier; a motor reaching it trips and cannot run.\nAll source wires/TVS/diode/shunt must be in the high-current loop. Short MOSFET path and Kelvin RSH sense routing are mandatory PCB constraints."
	(at 40 265 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "2fdd69ac-6a0b-4993-a0a4-abbc414ebd76")
)
	(text "DESIGN CALCULATIONS (datasheet limits, not a physical result)\nAt 125W/24V: I=5.208A. IRF5210PbF RDS(on) max 60mΩ @ VGS=−10V ⇒ Q1 or Q4 Pcond=I²R=1.63W at 25°C rating point. At INA trip 8.10A, P=3.94W only until cutoff.\nRSH1 5mΩ: P=0.136W nominal; 0.328W at 8.10A; specified ≥3W. INA300 offset max must be included in final threshold tolerance.\nD1 MBR20100CTG: 20A total (two 10A legs); 100V. D2 maximum clamp 69.4V: K_V Q1/Q4=100/69.4=1.44; D1=100/69.4=1.44; D2 standoff K_V=43/30=1.43. K_I at 8.10A: Q1/Q4 ≥40/8.10=4.94; D1 20/8.10=2.47. Thus K≥1.30 at defined interface; K_P shunt=3/0.328=9.15.\nNo SOA/thermal acceptance for an unknown motor transient is claimed: test must establish actual start current, current waveforms, MOSFET/diode/TVS temperature and supply dip before integration."
	(at 230 225 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
	(uuid "2b45b06d-6d7b-4858-ab7f-2787cb2a4aaf")
)
